    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43805" root="&#xA;                        نبع&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَبْعٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>The tree so-called:</i> see an ex. of its n.
un. in a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَحَوَّفَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَخَوَّفَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَبْعٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَوْحَطٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِرْيَانٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَتْحٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَبْعَانِ</span>
The <i>two shafts</i> of a cart: so called because
they were commonly made of wood of the tree
called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَبْع</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَادَّةٌ</span>.

